51:- `orchestrator`, `patch`, `review`, `linearize`, and `locks` define core workflow behavior.
62:- Command orchestration: `CommandChat`, `CommandChatResult`, `ProcessCommand`, `CliError`.
76:2. Core workflows live in `src/cli.rs`, `src/orchestrator.rs`, `src/patch.rs`, `src/review.rs`,
185:- orchestrator, patch, review, and linearizer coordination,
193:- `CommandChat::handle_line` for processing command lines such as `new`, `chat`, `review`, and
201:`CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.
216:- background launch/send/review workers,
218:- review startup, automatic per-patch-agent review routing, reviewer-session creation, and
219:  reviewed-commit bookkeeping,
223:loading state. A user-agent response becomes review-ready only when the orchestrator transcript shows
227:review readiness. Repository build, test, format, and required-check commands run only through
238:Review bookkeeping has three scopes. The controller records a launch-time review baseline for each
239:patch agent, tracks the latest reviewed hash for that patch agent so the same agent head is not
240:reviewed twice, and asks reviewers to inspect every provisional commit from the active baseline
241:through the latest patch-agent commit. `CommandChat` also keeps the ordered exact review targets that
242:completed review during the active instance, and those targets form the linearizer handoff. This lets
243:one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier
244:reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.
248:lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching
261:- `start_review` to create or resume reviewer sessions for explicit history-wide review and stream
262:  reviewer output.
277:`CommandTranscriptLine` carries one new command transcript line. `AgentStatusUpdated` carries
284:spawning, session naming, review lookup, loading bookkeeping, or orchestrator event routing.
367:`src/review.rs::GitHistory` reads latest agent commits from repository history, builds cumulative
368:review targets for a patch agent since a launch or reviewed baseline, and resolves agent metadata
369:commits by exact hash. `ReviewCoordinator<B>` launches reviewer agents against those review targets
370:and loops until the reviewer reports no findings or the configured maximum round count is reached.
371:`CommandChat` resolves reviewer `@work-leaf` directives, such as file reads, before interpreting
372:reviewer output as findings. `CommandChat` and `WorkLeafController` keep a stable
373:`review-<agent-id>` reviewer identity for each patch agent and skip latest agent heads that have
374:already completed review. `AgentCommit`, `ReviewResult`, and `ReviewError` are the public review
375:workflow types. `WorkLeafController` scopes automatic review after a patch agent reports done to the
376:patch agent that produced the provisional commit; explicit review commands use the history-wide
377:review target lookup.
383:exact commits recorded as reviewed in the current command-chat or controller instance; unrelated
384:historical agent metadata commits are outside the linearizer scope unless the user explicitly reviews
385:or adds them in that session. When one patch-agent id completes multiple reviewed commits in one
386:active instance, each reviewed hash is listed independently for the linearizer.
